      "summaryMarkdown": "WSL-1 holds. `LINUX_BINARY` is `$HOME/.rayx/bin/rayx` for the probe, the copy override and the inner `setup`. A non-matching version runs `set -o pipefail; curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf <v<version>/rayx-cli-installer.sh> | env -u RAYX_HOME sh && test -x <binary>` through `--exec bash -lc`; hand extraction into `~/.local/bin` is gone. Checked against the s1 generated installer: it has no prompts or /dev/tty reads (only `read -r RECEIPT` from a heredoc), installs to `$RAYX_HOME/bin` else `$HOME/.rayx/bin` (so dropping RAYX_HOME matches LINUX_BINARY), writes the receipt, edits PATH profiles itself, and `pipefail` makes a failed curl fail the step. The unsupported-architecture check precedes any download with the existing message; a matching version is not reinstalled. `wsl_install` (8) and `wsl_plan` (18) pass and assert the real script text and argv. The print-mode test is a sound proxy: `Runner::query` rejects interactive specs and is the only call that runs for real in print mode, and every mutating command (install, copy, inner setup, `--install`) is asserted interactive.",
